T*
(This text-only PDF is a concise overview prepared for the online research portfolio. It) Tj
T*
(presents the central motivation, modelling approach, results, limitations and future work of) Tj
T*
(the full M.Sc. thesis. The original submitted thesis contains the complete figures, tables,) Tj
T*
(equations and bibliography.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(ABSTRACT) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The thesis investigates the optical design of an indium zinc oxide / silver / indium zinc) Tj
T*
(oxide \(IZO/Ag/IZO\) multilayer as a transparent conducting electrode for photovoltaic) Tj
T*
(devices. Conventional transparent conducting oxides face a trade-off between optical) Tj
T*
(transmission and electrical conductivity. An oxide-metal-oxide structure can use an) Tj
T*
(ultrathin metal layer for lateral conduction while the surrounding dielectric layers are) Tj
T*
(designed to improve optical transmission through interference and admittance matching.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SETFOS simulations were used to study transmission, reflection and absorption while) Tj
T*
(systematically varying the thickness of the IZO and silver layers. Python-based analysis was) Tj
T*
(used to calculate wavelength-averaged transmission, transmitted photon flux and theoretical) Tj
T*
(short-circuit-current limits under the AM1.5G spectrum. The work also examined sheet) Tj
T*
(resistance and Haacke's figure of merit to avoid treating optical transmission as the only) Tj
T*
(design criterion.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A central part of the thesis was the treatment of ultrathin silver. Bulk optical constants) Tj
T*
(are not automatically valid for sub-10 nm films because the metal may grow as islands before) Tj
T*
(forming a continuous layer. Thickness-dependent behaviour was interpreted using a) Tj
T*
(Drude-based correction together with literature on Volmer-Weber growth, localized surface) Tj
T*
(plasmon resonance and wetting-layer-assisted continuity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The idealised simulations identified IZO\(45 nm\)/Ag\(8 nm\)/IZO\(60 nm\) for the 300-800 nm range) Tj
T*
(and IZO\(45 nm\)/Ag\(8 nm\)/IZO\(40 nm\) for the 300-1300 nm range as promising optical designs.) Tj
T*
(These simulated improvements are theoretical design limits, not direct predictions of) Tj
T*
(fabricated-device performance. Real structures introduce surface roughness, thickness) Tj
T*
(non-uniformity, scattering, grain boundaries, interface diffusion, imperfect film continuity) Tj
T*
(and differences between assumed and measured optical constants.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. RESEARCH MOTIVATION) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Transparent conducting electrodes must transmit light while carrying current. Increasing) Tj
T*
(oxide thickness may reduce sheet resistance but can also increase optical loss. Reducing) Tj
T*
(thickness can improve some optical properties while weakening lateral conductivity. An) Tj
T*
(oxide-metal-oxide stack offers another design space: a thin metal layer supports conduction,) Tj
T*
(and the upper and lower oxide layers modify the optical field.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The project initially began as a transparent-electrode study for tandem solar cells. During) Tj
T*
