(the work, the emphasis shifted increasingly toward photonics and light-matter interaction.) Tj
T*
(The questions that became most engaging were how nanoscale thickness changes reshape the) Tj
T*
(spectrum, how the optical constants of ultrathin materials differ from bulk values, how) Tj
T*
(fields are distributed inside a multilayer, and how an ideal optical model should be) Tj
T*
(connected to fabrication constraints.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. OPTICAL DESIGN APPROACH) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The optical response of the multilayer was modelled using SETFOS. Thickness sweeps were) Tj
T*
(carried out for the top IZO, intermediate Ag and bottom IZO layers. The following quantities) Tj
T*
(were considered:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Spectral transmission, reflection and absorption.) Tj
T*
(- Average transmission in wavelength ranges relevant to single-junction and tandem devices.) Tj
T*
(- AM1.5G-weighted transmitted photon flux.) Tj
T*
(- Theoretical short-circuit-current limit, used as an optical comparison metric.) Tj
T*
(- Approximate sheet resistance of the multilayer.) Tj
T*
(- Haacke's figure of merit, combining transparency and conductivity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Python was used for data processing and comparison between candidate structures. The) Tj
T*
(workflow was designed to identify optical mechanisms and promising thickness combinations) Tj
T*
(rather than to claim that ideal simulated gains would be reproduced unchanged after) Tj
T*
(fabrication.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. ULTRATHIN SILVER AND NON-BULK OPTICAL RESPONSE) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Silver films below approximately 10-15 nm can be discontinuous. During early growth,) Tj
T*
(deposited atoms may form separated islands. As thickness increases, the islands connect and) Tj
T*
(eventually form a continuous conducting film. This transition affects both optical and) Tj
T*
(electrical behaviour.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The thesis therefore did not treat bulk silver constants as universally valid. A Drude-based) Tj
T*
(approach was used to explore thickness-dependent damping and optical response, supported by) Tj
T*
(literature on island growth, percolation, localized plasmon resonances and wetting layers. A) Tj
T*
(thin germanium wetting layer was considered in relation to improved continuity of ultrathin) Tj
T*
(silver.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This analysis also highlighted an important experimental point: a nominal thickness does not) Tj
T*
(uniquely determine performance. Deposition rate, substrate condition, vacuum quality,) Tj
T*
(surface energy, wetting layer, roughness and post-deposition history can all alter the) Tj
T*
(morphology and therefore the measured optical constants.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. SIMULATED DESIGNS AND INTERPRETATION) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(For the 300-800 nm wavelength range, the simulation identified an IZO\(45 nm\)/Ag\(8 nm\)/IZO\(60) Tj
T*
(nm\) structure as a strong candidate. Relative to the simulated 140 nm IZO reference, the) Tj
T*
(model indicated an 8.55 percent increase in the theoretical short-circuit-current cap.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(For the broader 300-1300 nm range, an IZO\(45 nm\)/Ag\(8 nm\)/IZO\(40 nm\) design gave a simulated) Tj
T*
(13.06 percent improvement in wavelength-averaged transmission and a 6.17 percent improvement) Tj
T*
(in the theoretical current cap relative to the chosen reference.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(These percentages describe the output of an idealised optical comparison. They should not be) Tj
T*
(interpreted as guaranteed gains after deposition or as direct efficiency improvements in a) Tj
T*
