(complete solar cell. Fabricated films typically show smaller gains because the real stack) Tj
T*
(differs from the ideal model. Important causes include:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Incomplete or non-uniform silver coverage.) Tj
T*
(- Surface and interface roughness.) Tj
T*
(- Grain-boundary and defect-related electrical losses.) Tj
T*
(- Thickness variation across the substrate.) Tj
T*
(- Scattering and absorption not fully represented by the optical data.) Tj
T*
(- Interdiffusion and chemical changes at interfaces.) Tj
T*
(- Differences between literature optical constants and the deposited films.) Tj
T*
(- Additional parasitic absorption in a complete device stack.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The value of the simulation is therefore to reveal optical headroom, identify sensitive) Tj
T*
(parameters and reduce the experimental search space. Measured optical constants, morphology) Tj
T*
(and device data should be returned to the model in later design iterations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. ELECTRICAL AND FIGURE-OF-MERIT ANALYSIS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Optical transmission alone is insufficient for evaluating a transparent electrode. The) Tj
T*
(silver layer can strongly reduce lateral resistance, but only if the film is sufficiently) Tj
T*
(continuous. The thesis compared approximate sheet resistance with optical performance and) Tj
T*
(evaluated Haacke's figure of merit.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The simulated optimized stacks showed a two-to-fourfold enhancement in the figure of merit) Tj
T*
(compared with the selected single-layer reference under the assumptions used. As with the) Tj
T*
(optical results, this represents model-based potential. Experimental sheet resistance) Tj
T*
(depends strongly on morphology, contact quality and the electrical behaviour of the) Tj
T*
(interfaces.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. DEPOSITION-METHOD ANALYSIS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The thesis compared thermal evaporation and magnetron sputtering for ultrathin silver) Tj
T*
(deposition. A geometric material-utilisation estimate suggested that sputtering could) Tj
T*
(require approximately 24 times less target mass per deposition than the selected evaporation) Tj
T*
(configuration because of reduced angular loss and improved confinement of the deposited) Tj
T*
(flux.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This calculation is a tool-specific approximation, not a universal ratio for all evaporation) Tj
T*
(and sputtering systems. Actual utilisation depends on source geometry, target size, throw) Tj
T*
(distance, shielding, deposition area and operating conditions. The comparison nevertheless) Tj
T*
(showed why process efficiency and scalability should be considered alongside optical) Tj
T*
(performance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7. EXPERIMENTAL FOUNDATION) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The research was supported by hands-on experience with RF magnetron sputtering, metal) Tj
T*
(evaporation, cleanroom processing, vacuum handling, UV-Vis-NIR spectroscopy,) Tj
T*
(four-point-probe measurements and profilometry. This experimental exposure informed the) Tj
T*
(interpretation of the simulations and made clear why ideal layer thicknesses must be tested) Tj
T*
(against process capability and film morphology.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(8. MAIN LESSONS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Light management in a transparent electrode is a coupled optical, electrical and materials) Tj
T*
